From: openHarmony PC porting
Subject: [PATCH] Align RRULE test fixtures with libical >= 4 part ordering

libical 4.0's icalrecurrencetype_as_string() emits the RRULE parts in
the order they were stored (verified by round-trip:
"FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=4;BYMONTHDAY=20" stays unchanged), while the
libical 3.x series used by upstream CI normalized the output to the
fixed RFC order (BYMONTHDAY before BYMONTH). Per RFC 5545 the order of
the RRULE parts carries no semantics, and libkgapi's own fixtures are
already inconsistent on this (event2_create_response.txt, coming from
the Google side, uses BYMONTH before BYMONTHDAY, and libkgapi
round-trips it faithfully). Adapt the two expected-request fixtures to
the libical 4 ordering so the upstream expectations match reality on
OHOS.
---
--- a/autotests/calendar/data/event2_create_request.txt
+++ b/autotests/calendar/data/event2_create_request.txt
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
     "email": "MockAccount"
   },
   "recurrence": [
-    "RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTHDAY=20;BYMONTH=4"
+    "RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=4;BYMONTHDAY=20"
   ],
   "reminders": {
     "overrides": [
--- a/autotests/calendar/data/event2_modify_request.txt
+++ b/autotests/calendar/data/event2_modify_request.txt
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
     "email": "MockAccount"
   }, 
   "recurrence": [
-    "RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTHDAY=20;BYMONTH=4"
+    "RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=4;BYMONTHDAY=20"
   ], 
   "reminders": {
     "overrides": [
